{
  "title": "Accepted 1000-Hz audiometry repeat variability does not establish added hearing-difficulty prediction across NHANES cycles",
  "abstract": "Among 3,816 source and 4,263 target complete-case adults, adding mean absolute bilateral 1000-Hz repeat difference did not establish improved hearing-difficulty prediction across NHANES 2011\u201312 and 2015\u201316: weighted log-loss difference 0.000003503, joint PSU-bootstrap 95% interval [-0.000821488,0.001447151]. This is an exploratory, protocol-conditioned negative result, not evidence that repeat variability has no physiological information.",
